# Algorithm Logic and Visualization Explanation

## Algorithm Logic

Merge Sort divides the input array into two halves repeatedly.
It sorts each half and then combines the sorted halves.
Its time complexity is O(n log n) in the best, average, and worst cases.

Quick Sort selects a pivot and partitions the array around it.
It then recursively sorts the left and right partitions.
Its average time complexity is O(n log n), while its worst-case
time complexity is O(n²).

